    "schedule": "A/B order alternates between pairs. Within measured pairs, the five-bracket order rotates by pair index modulo five. The CSV preserves every observation, including the warmups and extremes.",
    "analysis": "For each bracket, compute B minus A within each measured pair and take the median of the 24 differences. The descriptive interval uses the 2.5th and 97.5th percentile ranks from 10,000 deterministic bootstrap medians that resample blocks of two adjacent pairs. The AB, BA, first-half and second-half values are separate medians of the same differences. Sign counts use all 24 measured pairs. The estimates exclude warmups.",
    "bootstrap_reproduction": {
      "counter_start": 0,
      "text_prefix": "ptg/rate-study/bootstrap/rate/20261126/",
      "draw": "Append the decimal counter and use the first eight SHA-256 bytes as an unsigned big-endian integer. Increment the counter for every draw. Reject values at or above floor(2^64 / 23) times 23. Use accepted values modulo 23 to pick the first index of an adjacent pair block.",
      "blocks_per_resample": 12,
      "resamples": 10000,
      "sorted_interval_indices_zero_based": [249, 9749]
    },
    "workload_scope": "The adapter uses real Limiter operations with ordered synthetic keys, fixed tick values and scripted liveness. A keeps ordinary randomized HashMap seeding. B replaces the index type. Setup and post-bracket checks verify ordered entries, index positions, decisions, survivors and ordered summaries outside the measured brackets. These workloads run in opt-level 3 test binaries.",
    "original_run": {
      "outer_native_exit": 0,
      "controller_native_exit": 0,
      "original_app_event_duration_seconds": 9.4554871,
      "timing_scope": "The original app event records carrier duration. Adapter timings use their own brackets."
    }
